Feature: §16 FASE5 assert — the teko::assert compare+panic family runs pure Teko over the migrated panic, off the C seed

  Scenario: assert_battery_passes — every family (is_true/eq_i64/ne_i64/ordering/eq_u64/eq_f64/eq_str/ne_str/str_contains/len_eq/bytes_eq/is_present/is_absent/is_ok/is_error) returns without panic
    Given env = ["TEKO_BACKEND=c"]
    When built and run
    Then stdout pattern = "assert-battery: ok"
    And exit = 0

  Scenario: eq_i64_mismatch_traps — a failing eq_i64 panics through the Teko fail path, non-zero with the expected/got message
    Given source = "cases/eq_i64_mismatch.tks"
    Given env = ["TEKO_BACKEND=c"]
    When built and run
    Then it traps
    And stderr pattern = "assertion failed: eq_i64 — expected 42, got 41"

  Scenario: bytes_eq_mismatch_traps — a failing bytes_eq panics naming the first differing index
    Given source = "cases/bytes_eq_mismatch.tks"
    Given env = ["TEKO_BACKEND=c"]
    When built and run
    Then it traps
    And stderr pattern = "assertion failed: bytes_eq — expected byte 100 at index 2, got 99"
